 clear long-term change"},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 64\u00b0F was the 6th warmest November 10 high (tied) of 124 since 1900, the warmest since 2025.","t_yest":"November 10: warmer than 95% of years","p_yest":"The high of <strong>64\u00b0F</strong> was the 6th warmest November 10 high (tied) of 124 since 1900, the warmest since 2025. The normal high for the date is 51\u00b0F, and the record is 71\u00b0F (2016). The low of <strong>26\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 10.","t_rec":"Record highs and lows, by the decade that set them","p_rec":"If Klamath Falls' climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Klamath Falls has set <strong>111 standing record lows</strong>, more than the 77 that chance alone would give, and <strong>98 record highs</strong>, more than the 78 that chance alone would give. The 1990s hold the most record highs of any decade (53). Klamath Falls' all-time high is 104\u00b0F, on August 7, 1972.","t_chg":"Klamath Falls' nights have cooled. Its days warmed over the long run.","p_chg":"Across 115 complete years: Klamath Falls' average low has fallen <strong class='sig'>\u22120.13\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range \u22120.22 to \u22120.04), about \u22121.6\u00b0F since 1901. Klamath Falls' average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.17\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.08 to +0.26), about +2.1\u00b0F since 1901.","t_mon":"Lows rose in none; 5 months fell. Highs rose in 2 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Klamath Falls' yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (\u22120.18 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 11.5 inches a year. The wettest year was 1996 (21.05 in); the driest, 2013 (5.59 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 7 daily record highs, 6 daily record lows"}}